  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1208 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nClouds cleared out early yesterday, setting the stage for efficient \nradiational cooling early this morning. Low temperatures will likely \ndip into the mid to upper 40s inland early this morning and \nWednesday morning. Rain-free conditons prevail this week as a mid-\nlevel ridge continues to impact South Texas. Gradual increase in \ndaily temperatures as the weekend approaches, peaking Saturday with \nhighs possibly reaching into the 80's for the Brush Country and \nsouthern Coastal Plains. Low temperatures remain in the mid to low \n50s through the week, and by Friday increase to the 60s for the rest \nof the weekend. A mid- level trough forms over the northern gulf and \nmid-level shortwaves move through the area associated with a deeper \ntrough over the Four Corners region, allowing for low rain chances \nto return late Saturday into Sunday.\nWinds are expected to remain light and stay at a northeasterly flow, \nbut onshore flow returns this weekend with a more east to \nsoutheasterly flow.\n\nMinor coastal flooding conditions are still favorable through \nmajority of the week, as well as a moderate to high rip current risk \nwith long swell periods of 8-10 seconds and light to moderate \nnortheasterly flow remain.",
